Description: Take the first free HTTP port from 8200 when none is set
 Clients find a DLNA server through SSDP discovery, which carries the HTTP
 port in its LOCATION URL, so the port need not be fixed. Without a port
 setting (port=, -p, --port), minidlnad now tries 8200, 8201, ... (up to 100
 ports) and uses the first free one. A port that is set is used exactly and
 minidlnad exits if it is busy.
 .
 The HTTP socket is now opened in init(), after daemonizing, so that without
 -P the pid file can be named after the port (minidlna-<port>.pid) and one
 user can run several instances. Instances on a port other than 8200 get a
 UUID that includes the port and, unless friendly_name is set, a name ending
 in "[<port>]", so clients don't merge them with the instance on 8200.
Forwarded: no
Last-Update: 2026-10-21
